sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/aristotle-pa01-08> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Animals should be classified into the natural groups that mankind instinctively recognizes, such as Birds and Fishes, each defined by many differentiae together, and not by successive two-way division on a single character.";
    dc:type "conceptual";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Natural groups are marked by many differentiae, not by dichotomy";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Aristotle, On the Parts of Animals (De Partibus Animalium), Book I, Part 3; translated by William Ogle, The Works of Aristotle Translated into English, ed. J. A. Smith and W. D. Ross, Oxford: Clarendon Press, vol. V (1912). Scope: classification of all animals"
}
